  ## Findings
  
  ### [Critical] kurojisho.python.sql-string-built
  
  `api/app.py:16`: SQL statement built by string concatenation or formatting is passed to a query call.
  
  | | |
  |---|---|
  | Reported by | bandit, semgrep (tool severity High) |
  | Weakness | CWE-89 |
  | Decided by | TRI-01 |
  | Reachability | R4: untrusted input flows from api/app.py::http GET /users to this call |
  | Exploitability | E2: tool severity High |
  | Business impact | I3: asset public-api: tier 1, PCI, PII; exposure internet |
  | Entry points | api/app.py::http GET /users |
  
  Why:
  - TRI-01: Reachable from an entry point, exploitable, high business impact
  
  Fix: **Use parameterised queries**. Pass user input as bound parameters (placeholders) instead of building the SQL string. Where identifiers must vary (table or column names), choose them from a fixed allowlist.
  
  Verify:
  - Confirm no query at this location is built by concatenation or string formatting.
  - Send a quote character and a boolean payload through the entry point; the query must not change shape.
  
  ### [Critical] kurojisho.python.code-eval
  
  `api/app.py:22`: eval or exec runs a string as code; with untrusted input this is code execution.
  
  | | |
  |---|---|
  | Reported by | semgrep (tool severity High) |
  | Weakness | CWE-95 |
  | Decided by | TRI-01 |
  | Reachability | R4: untrusted input flows from api/app.py::http GET /calc to this call |
  | Exploitability | E2: tool severity High |
  | Business impact | I3: asset public-api: tier 1, PCI, PII; exposure internet |
  | Entry points | api/app.py::http GET /calc |
  
  Why:
  - TRI-01: Reachable from an entry point, exploitable, high business impact
  
  Fix: **Do not evaluate untrusted input as code**. Remove the dynamic evaluation. Parse the input as data (a literal parser, JSON, or an explicit expression grammar) and map allowed operations to code yourself.
  
  Verify:
  - Confirm no eval/exec/template-from-string call receives request data.
  
  ### [Critical] kurojisho.python.shell-command
  
  `api/app.py:28`: Command is run through a shell; untrusted input leads to command injection.
  
  | | |
  |---|---|
  | Reported by | bandit, semgrep (tool severity High) |
  | Weakness | CWE-78 |
  | Decided by | TRI-01 |
  | Reachability | R4: untrusted input flows from api/app.py::http GET /ping to this call |
  | Exploitability | E2: tool severity High |
  | Business impact | I3: asset public-api: tier 1, PCI, PII; exposure internet |
  | Entry points | api/app.py::http GET /ping |
  
  Why:
  - TRI-01: Reachable from an entry point, exploitable, high business impact
  
  Fix: **Do not pass untrusted input to a shell**. Call the program directly with an argument list and no shell. If a shell is unavoidable, quote every argument with the platform's quoting function and validate it against an allowlist first.
  
  Verify:
  - Confirm the call uses an argument list and no shell.
  - Send shell metacharacters (; | $()) through the entry point; no extra command may run.
  
