  ### [Medium] kurojisho.java.weak-hash
  
  `java/src/main/java/com/demo/Dao.java:24`: MD5 and SHA-1 are broken for security purposes.
  
  | | |
  |---|---|
  | Reported by | semgrep (tool severity Medium) |
  | Weakness | CWE-327 |
  | Decided by | no rule matched |
  | Reachability | R0: no entry point is known to reach this code |
  | Exploitability | E1: tool severity Medium |
  | Business impact | I0: asset batch: tier 4; exposure none |
  | Flags | no_rule_matched |
  
  Why:
  - No triage rule covers this finding; the tool's severity is kept
  
  Fix: **Replace the weak algorithm**. Use SHA-256 or stronger for integrity, and a password hashing function (Argon2id, scrypt, bcrypt) for passwords. Plan a migration for stored values.
  
  Verify:
  - Confirm no MD5/SHA-1/DES use remains on a security-relevant path.
  
